In this task, I launched a full vulnerability scan on my local Windows system using Nessus Essentials. After setting up the scan, I started it from the Scans → My Scans section. Nessus proceeded to run a comprehensive evaluation that included port scanning, service detection, SSL/TLS checks, SMB analysis, configuration reviews, and identification of software vulnerabilities. The scan operated automatically without the need for further input and took several minutes to finish. When it completed, the results were stored and made available for detailed analysis in the following task.
